<body>
    <h1>Introduction to Vision Framework</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>The Vision Framework is Apple=E2=80=99s main tool for recognizin=
g patterns in images. It was launched in 2017 as part of iOS 11 and was cre=
ated to supply developers with a set of tools for handling computer vision =
tasks.</p>
<p>It allows advanced features to be integrated directly into on-device app=
s. Things like face detection and recognition, text identification, object =
tracking, and pose analysis can all be done without needing to create algor=
ithms from scratch.</p>
<p>To make this possible, Apple added GPUs and the Neural Engine into its h=
ardware, which is responsible for a big part of the energy efficiency when =
running machine learning solutions natively.</p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>Likewise, other hardware accelerators have also evolved and contribute i=
n making this technology more powerful and efficient.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"IntroductiontoVisionFramework-StructureandFunctioning">Structure =
and Functioning</h3>
<p>The Vision Framework, just like CoreML, was built with a <strong>modular=
 architecture</strong> that eases the implementation and customization of c=
omputer vision tasks. Each feature =E2=80=93 whether it=E2=80=99s face dete=
ction, text recognition, or object tracking =E2=80=93 is packed into a spec=
ific request. These requests are processed by dedicated handlers, which let=
s developers combine different tasks based on the application=E2=80=99s nee=
ds. This modular approach not only makes development simpler, but also help=
s reuse components and speeds up the process of building robust and customi=
zed solutions.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-cen=
ter-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embed=
ded-image image-center" alt=3D"Untitled - Frame 1 (1).jpg" width=3D"468" lo=
ading=3D"lazy" src=3D"8e06f0c16ca1ffbea03b90a71ec795fa66bcbe0611189b1288daf=
e9b51fd613a" data-image-src=3D"https://developeracademy.atlassian.net/wiki/=
download/attachments/1208877064/Untitled%20-%20Frame%201%20(1).jpg?version=
=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1750692274175&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-height=3D"666" data-width=3D"1499" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"=
0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1208877076" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1=
" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-ali=
as=3D"Untitled - Frame 1 (1).jpg" data-base-url=3D"https://developeracademy=
.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/jpeg" data-=
linked-resource-container-id=3D"1208877064" data-linked-resource-container-=
version=3D"1" data-media-id=3D"15fa5f4a-720d-4764-83e6-43579d673b80" data-m=
edia-type=3D"file" height=3D"207"></span>
<p>In the image above, we have an example of how the execution pipeline wor=
ks when using the Vision Framework:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Image Input</strong></p>
<p>The user either takes a picture or selects one that has faces in it. The=
 image gets loaded into the app and is sent for processing by the Vision Fr=
amework.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Request</strong></p>
<p>The app creates a request (<code>VNDetectFaceRectanglesRequest</code>) t=
o let the Vision Framework know it wants to find faces in the image.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Handler</strong></p>
<p>A handler (<code>VNImageRequestHandler</code>) receives the request and =
processes the image using Vision=E2=80=99s internal algorithms to detect fa=
ces.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Response</strong></p>
<p>The framework returns a response with the coordinates of the faces it fo=
und in the image. These results can be used to highlight faces visually or =
for further analysis.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Visualization Result</strong></p>
<p>The app can, for example, draw boxes around the detected faces and show =
the processed image to the user.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>When it comes to <strong>processing images and videos</strong>, the fram=
ework works in a highly optimized and real-time way. As soon as it gets vis=
ual data, it applies advanced algorithms to analyze each frame or image, id=
entifying patterns, recognizing text, and detecting objects.</p>
<p>Its <strong>integration with machine learning and deep learning</strong>=
 is another fundamental pillar of the Vision Framework. Models trained to i=
nterpret and analyze visual information are incorporated into the process, =
allowing the framework to perform complex analyses with high precision. Thi=
s synergy between computer vision algorithms and machine learning enables t=
he extraction of detailed information and the identification of nuances tha=
t traditional methods would have a hard time to capture. As a result, devel=
opers can focus on innovation and on creating smarter experiences, while th=
e framework handles all the technical challenges of image and video analysi=
s behind the scenes.</p>
<p>In short, the combination of modular architecture, real-time processing,=
 and advanced integration with machine learning makes the Vision Framework =
a strong and flexible tool for building apps that rely on the interpretatio=
n of visual content. This structure not only enables the creation of effici=
ent solutions but also allows for continuous and seamless adaptation to new=
 features.</p>
<h3 id=3D"IntroductiontoVisionFramework-MainFeatures">Main Features</h3>
<p>The Vision Framework offers a solid set of features focused on analyzing=
 and interpreting images and videos. These tools allow developers to add ad=
vanced computer vision resources to their apps, providing smarter and more =
interactive experience for users. Some of the main features include:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Face Detection and Recognition</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p>Face detection is one of the most popular features in the Vision Framewo=
rk. It can identify the presence and position of faces in images and videos=
. On top of that, the framework also offers face recognition, which enables=
 the differentiation between individuals, making it useful for authenticati=
on and personalized experiences. Some practical uses include unlocking devi=
ces, augmented reality (AR) filters, and security systems. It can be used w=
ith <code>VNDetectFaceRectanglesRequest</code> (Face detection) and <code>V=
NRecognizeFacesRequest</code> (Facial recognition).</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Text Recognition (OCR)</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p>The Vision Framework includes an optical character recognition (OCR) sys=
tem that pulls text from images and videos with high accuracy. This feature=
 can be used to scan documents, read license plates, identify barcodes, or =
even to auto-translate text captured by camera. It uses machine learning to=
 ensure efficient interpretation, even under challenging conditions such as=
 tilted or handwritten texts. It can be used with <code>VNRecognizeTextRequ=
est</code>.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Object Tracking and Pose Analysis</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p>Object tracking allows an app to identify and follow specific elements a=
s they move through a video. This feature is widely used in sports apps, mo=
nitoring tools, and gesture-based interfaces. The framework also supports h=
uman pose analysis, which helps detect body structure and movements in real=
 time, something essential in fitness apps, games, and augmented reality ex=
periences. It can be used with <code>VNTrackObjectRequest</code> (Object tr=
acking) and <code>VNDetectHumanBodyPoseRequest</code> (Pose analysis).</p>
<h3 id=3D"IntroductiontoVisionFramework-PerformanceandEfficiency">Performan=
ce and Efficiency</h3>
<p>The Vision Framework was built to deliver high <strong>performance and e=
fficiency</strong>, making sure computer vision tasks run fast, accurately,=
 and with optimal energy use. To do that, it takes advantage of the local p=
rocessing power in Apple products, reducing the need to rely on outside ser=
vers, which means better privacy and lower latency for apps. This setup is =
perfect for apps that need to process visuals in real time.</p>
<p>One of the main advantages of the Vision Framework is its ability to run=
 computer vision tasks directly on the device <strong>(on-device processing=
)</strong>. That means no internet connection is needed to analyze images a=
nd videos, which leads to faster and more efficient performance. Further, o=
n-device processing also enhances user privacy, since the visual data doesn=
=E2=80=99t have to be sent to external servers. Applications such as facial=
 recognition for Face ID unlocking, object tracking, and OCR benefit from t=
his approach, delivering near-instant results.</p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>To push performance even further, the Vision Framework integrates with t=
he <strong>Apple Neural Engine (ANE)</strong>, which is a special component=
 of Apple=E2=80=99s chips developed to boost machine learning tasks.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>The <strong>Apple Neural Engine</strong> makes it possible to run comput=
er vision models with great energy efficiency. It reduces the load on the C=
PU and GPU, which means that apps can perform complex tasks, like face dete=
ction or text recognition, quickly and without compromising the device=E2=
=80=99s battery life. Using the Neural Engine allows for faster and more ac=
curate inference in custom machine learning models integrated into the fram=
ework.</p>
<p>This combination of performance tuning makes the Vision Framework a robu=
st solution for a solid range of scenarios, from security and authenticatio=
n applications to augmented reality and visual assistants. The efficiency i=
n task execution means that developers can create sophisticated experiences=
 without compromising the responsiveness or usability of their apps.</p>
<h3 id=3D"IntroductiontoVisionFramework-VisionKitvsVisionFramework:WhichOne=
toUse?">VisionKit vs Vision Framework: Which One to Use?</h3>
<p><strong>VisionKit</strong> and <strong>Vision Framework</strong> are App=
le=E2=80=99s frameworks built to analyze images and videos, both using mach=
ine learning to interpret visual information. However, they serve different=
 purposes: <strong>VisionKit</strong> is focused on scanning documents and =
extracting structured information, like text and machine-readable codes. It=
=E2=80=99s ideal for apps that need to scan receipts, read QR codes, or pul=
l text from documents fast. <strong>Vision Framework</strong>, on the other=
 hand, has a broader focus. It offers advanced tools like <strong>image cla=
ssification, object detection, face detection, object tracking, and pose an=
alysis</strong>, making it the go-to for apps that deal with AR, pattern re=
cognition in images, or real-time visual monitoring.</p>
<p>Even though they=E2=80=99re different, both frameworks share features li=
ke <strong>text recognition (OCR)</strong> and can complement each other. F=
or example, an app might use <strong>VisionKit</strong> to capture a docume=
nt, then <strong>Vision Framework</strong> to check for signatures or water=
marks.</p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>When it comes to compatibility, both use Apple=E2=80=99s machine learnin=
g tech and can integrate with <strong>Core ML</strong>. That means custom m=
odels can be used for more specific pattern recognition. The choice between=
 them depends on how much control and flexibility is necessary: <strong>If =
the main goal is document scanning with a smooth workflow, VisionKit is the=
 best choice; For a more complex visual analysis, Vision Framework is more =
powerful.</strong></p>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"IntroductiontoVisionFramework-Conclusion">Conclusion</h3>
<p>The <strong>Vision Framework</strong> is a must-have tool for developers=
 who want to integrate advanced computer vision features to their apps. It =
can handle things like pattern recognition in images and videos, text analy=
sis, object tracking, and pose detection. Combined with efficient on-device=
 processing and the use of the <strong>Neural Engine</strong>, it=E2=80=99s=
 ideal for creating fast, accurate solutions with excellent energy performa=
nce.</p>
<p>Additionally, its modular architecture allows for flexibility and custom=
ization, making it easier to implement complex solutions without the need t=
o reinvent algorithms. The integration with <strong>deep learning and machi=
ne learning</strong> models enhances the accuracy and sophistication of ana=
lyses, allowing developers to focus on innovation.</p>
<p>In the end, the Vision Framework represents an efficient and complete pl=
atform for creating smart, interactive, and real-time visual experiences.</=
p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
